-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_62.sql (Isaiah 62) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 62 — ZION'S NEW NAME / the married land, the restoration crown. The divorced
-- wife of the prophets (Hosea's Lo-Ammi) is renamed and remarried: *thou shalt be called by a new
-- name, which the mouth of Yahuah (LORD) shall name* (62:2); *Thou shalt no more be termed
-- Forsaken... but thou shalt be called Hephzi-bah, and thy land Beulah: for Yahuah (LORD)
-- delighteth in thee, and thy land shall be married* (62:4); *as the bridegroom rejoiceth over the
-- bride, so shall thy Elohim (God) rejoice over thee* (62:5). This is NOT replacement — it is the
-- SAME scattered, divorced two-house wife restored: Forsaken/Desolate become Delighted-in/Married,
-- Lo-Ammi becomes Ammi. The new name is given to the overcomer (Rev 2:17 / 3:12); the bridegroom
-- is the Formed Son and the restored Yashar'el the bride (Rev 19:7 / 21:2); the coming One brings
-- his reward (62:11 → Rev 22:12); the holy people / redeemed are the peculiar people (62:12 →
-- 1 Peter 2:9-10).
-- Tag: isa62   Temp view: _s303_isa62_lookup
-- Sort band: base 27525, step 3 -> threads at 27525, 27528, 27531, 27534, 27537 (5 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','isaiah',62,v
--
